9
00:49:03,000 --> 00:49:09,000
Butterfield, played by Barry Del Sherman.

10
00:54:30,000 --> 00:54:36,000
Lord of Illusions is a 1995 American neo-noir supernatural horror film written and directed by Clive Barker, based
on his own short story The Last Illusion published in 1985 in the anthology Books of Blood Volume 6.

11
00:59:57,000 --> 01:00:03,000
The same story introduced Barker's occult detective Harry D'Amour, who
later appeared in several prose stories and comic books.

12
01:05:24,000 --> 01:05:30,000
Lord of Illusions is D'Amour's first onscreen appearance, with
the character portrayed by actor Scott Bakula.

13
01:10:51,000 --> 01:10:57,000
Other actors appearing in the film include Kevin J.

14
01:16:18,000 --> 01:16:24,000
O'Connor, Famke Janssen and Daniel von Bargen.

15
01:21:45,000 --> 01:21:51,000
The story features D'Amour, who has had several experiences with the supernatural, embarking on an
investigation involving a stage illusionist named Swann and a cult led by a sorcerer named Nix.

16
01:27:12,000 --> 01:27:18,000
Although Clive Barker decided to keep a few story elements and the same principal characters from "The Last Illusion", he otherwise
presented a new story for the movie and created a new villain, surprising several readers familiar with the original work.

17
01:32:39,000 --> 01:32:45,000
The film met with mixed reception and no further live-action
movies featuring Harry D'Amour were made.

18
01:38:06,000 --> 01:38:12,000
The film explores themes of supernatural, fanatic, resurrection, occult, sect.

19
01:43:33,000 --> 01:43:39,000
The tone is dark and emotional.
